<title>SINGAPORE: Shell Singapore restarts secondary units Mar 8.</title>
<headline>Shell Singapore restarts secondary units Mar 8.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Singapore has restarted its 11,000 tonne-per-day (82,000 barrel-per-day) thermal gas unit and a 4,400 tonne-per-day hydrocracker (32,780-bpd) on March 8, a company spokeswoman said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Shell shutdown half of the thermal gas oil unit on March 2 while the entire hydrocracker unit was shut down on March 5, both due to unexpected technical problems.</p>
<p>&quot;Both units are back up to normal capacities,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Shell has a 435,000-bpd refinery at Pulau Bukom off the southern coast of Singapore.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
